From: Sebastian Gerke <Sebastian.Gerke@dlr.de>
Date: Mon, 9 Oct 2017 09:33:02 +0000
Subject: parallel comparison

See bugs.debian.org/878060

OpenMP parallelized comparison of two PDFs

* What led up to the situation?

     Comparison of two testsuitereports lasts more then a minute

* What exactly did you do

     I wrote a patch to minimize the time of comparison

* What was the outcome of this action?

     Now it only takes  a few seconds to compare two testsuitereports

[bap 2026-10-01: Only touch the GUI (status label, log, event loop) from
 the GUI thread, i.e., OpenMP thread 0.  Doing so from worker threads
 caused "QSocketNotifier: Can only be used with threads started with
 QThread" and "Cannot queue arguments of type 'QTextBlock'" warnings
 (#1041494) and could crash.  Also initialize the per-page results,
 which were left uninitialized for pages that failed to load or were
 skipped on cancel, report log lines in page order, keep partial results
 on cancel as the serial code did, and correct the count of pages
 compared.]
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/878060
